
Linear Regression Projects – Insurance Bill & House Price Prediction

This repository contains two practical machine learning projects:

🏥 Hospital Insurance Bill / Prediction System
🏠 House Price Prediction System

These projects demonstrate the use of machine learning techniques for solving real-world problems in healthcare and real estate domains.

 Project Structure
├── hospital.ipynb        # Hospital-related ML project
├── HousePrice.ipynb      # House price prediction model
└── README.md             # Documentation

Features
Data preprocessing and cleaning
Feature selection and transformation
Model training and evaluation
Real-world dataset handling
Visualization of results
 
Hospital Bill Project
 Description:

This project focuses on analyzing hospital-related data and building a model for prediction or decision-making (e.g., Insurance Bill prediction, patient analysis, or treatment recommendation depending on your implementation).

 Key Steps:
Data preprocessing
Handling missing values
Feature encoding
Model training
Prediction & evaluation
Possible Use Cases:
Bill prediction
Patient risk analysis
Hospital resource planning

House Price Prediction
📌 Description:

This project uses machine learning to predict house prices based on features like location, size, number of rooms, etc.

 Key Steps:
Data cleaning and preprocessing
Feature scaling
Model training (e.g., Linear Regression / ANN / etc.)
Model evaluation
 Evaluation Metrics:
Mean Absolute Error (MAE)
Mean Squared Error (MSE)
R² Score

Technologies Used
Python 🐍
NumPy
Pandas
Matplotlib / Seaborn
Scikit-learn (or mention if you used ANN/TensorFlow)
